# Copy to .env and adjust. Loaded automatically at startup (dotenv) by both `skein` and
# `skein-server`. Real environment variables always take precedence over this file.
# Full reference: docs/operating.md "Configuration".

# --- usually all you need ---
# Nothing. Managed repos (`skein add <url>`) need no configuration at all — run `skein login claude`
# once, add a repo, start `skein-server`, and everything below stays commented out.

# SKEIN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:7878             # where the cockpit listens

# --- legacy: the single-repo path, from before `skein add` existed ---
# These are only for a repo skein does NOT manage. If you are starting today you want none of them,
# and setting SKEIN_REGISTRY in particular makes an unreadable path a reported fault rather than a
# non-issue.
# SKEIN_REGISTRY=/abs/path/to/shared/.claude/sandboxes.json
# SKEIN_REPO=/abs/path/to/your/repo     # where git/gh run; relative *_CMD paths resolve here
# SKEIN_KIT="dev-sandbox/kit"           # kit that wires the shared store into the clone
# SKEIN_AGENT=claude                    # sbx agent for new boxes (claude | codex | …)
# SKEIN_STORE=/abs/shared/.claude       # shared store to mount; default = SKEIN_REGISTRY's dir
# SKEIN_LAUNCH_CMD="dev-sandbox/setup-sandbox.sh {branch}"   # delegate launch to a repo script

# --- optional (quote values with spaces) ---
# SKEIN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:7878             # server bind address
# SKEIN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=proxy.host      # extra WebSocket origins (loopback + *.ts.net always allowed)
# SKEIN_ATTACH_CMD="sbx run --name {name} -- --continue"
# SKEIN_SHELL_CMD="sbx exec -it {name} /bin/bash"
# SKEIN_STOP_CMD="sbx stop {name}"
# SKEIN_DESTROY_CMD="sbx rm -f {name}"
# SKEIN_AI=on                           # opt into rationed Haiku enrichment
